def verify_state_proofs(
    document: object, accounts: object, trust: object
) -> dict:
    """Offline-verify a batch ``POST /v1/accounts/attested-proofs`` document.

    ``document`` is the decoded response with the exact top-level key order
    ``state, proofs, auth``: ``state`` is the shared state-root document
    (``state_root, height, block_hash, account_count`` in that order),
    ``proofs`` is a non-empty list of account-state inclusion proofs (each in
    the exact single-proof shape) sorted by ascending account, and ``auth``
    is the one batch ``{key_version, signature}`` envelope. ``accounts`` is
    the caller-pinned non-empty list of distinct 64-lowercase-hex accounts;
    ``trust`` must carry an ``audit_signers`` list exactly as for
    :func:`verify_state_proof`.

    Verification, in order:

